sts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2020-03-17T19:45:07Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"fc2929"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/600268147","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/7097#issuecomment-600268147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/7097","id":600268147,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYwMDI2ODE0Nw==","user":{"login":"stari4ek","id":327778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNzc3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/327778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek","html_url":"https://github.com/stari4ek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stari4ek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-03-17T19:57:00Z","updated_at":"2020-03-17T19:57:00Z","body":"> I think this is working as intended. Can you elaborate why you think the documentation of onRenderedFirstFrame() is not matching the behaviour you see?\r\n\r\nSince it's the same stream, and first frame was rendered already (and notified with `onRenderedFirstFrame` ) and it's the same surface (_\"since setting the surface\"_) with same tracks selected (_\"since a video track was selected\"_). At least as exoplayer (`SimpleExoPlayer`) client I performed seek only.\r\n\r\n> I'm a bit confused around the mediaPos=0.00 which shows up in your logs above from BUFFERING and then goes back to 281.77 (if you think this is relevant, can you send me the uri to the media?).\r\n\r\nIt happens cause of seeking. I thought that this one is normal cause of https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/6562\r\n\r\n> However, my understanding of seekProcessed is, that the player has selected the next period to be played and updated the public playback position accordingly. No data is necessarily downloaded at this point and when needed this starts after updating the playback position.\r\n\r\nIn my case it worked totally different - cause current position was 0 when I checked it from `seekProcessed()` - i was going to adjust \"expected position after seek\" to real one.\r\n\r\nPlease note, that my stream is http progressive. Live (`isCurrentWindowLive()`) and not-seekable (`isCurrentWindowSeekable()`). \r\nThis is multicast mpeg-ts stream which goes through `udpxy` (udp to http proxy). It's in private network from my internet provider - so I cannot expose share it with you.\r\n\r\nHere is log when playback is started:\r\n```\r\n22:40:54.343 volume [eventTime=57.38, mediaPos=53.48, window=0, period=0, 0.0]\r\n22:40:54.384 timeline [eventTime=57.42, mediaPos=0.00, window=0, periodCount=0, windowCount=0, reason=PLAYLIST_CHANGED\r\n22:40:54.387 ]\r\n22:40:54.420 tracks [eventTime=57.46, mediaPos=0.00, window=0, []]\r\n22:40:54.454 loading [eventTime=57.48, mediaPos=0.00, window=0, fal